From 75e08445daf11e8f570a1cebf6557f9a0b1c9503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhang Junjie <zhangjunjie@actiontec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:42:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fix spurious STOMP restarts on transient mgmt IP loss

During a DHCP release/rebind cycle on the management interface the
IPv4 address transiently disappears while an IPv6 global address
remains. nu_ipaddr_has_interface_addr_changed() compares across
address families, so the remaining IPv6 address masked the IPv4 loss
and reported the address as changed. HandleStompSourceIPAddrChanges()
then restarted the STOMP connection (closing it with RST), and the
reconnect (DNS transient + retry backoff) lost any USP request the
controller sent in that window.

On the CDRouter prpl certification flow this deterministically killed
prpl_hl-api-cert.1.4 (the profile write-back includes DHCPv4.Client
SentOption writes that restart the DHCP request cycle) and made
prplos.1.2.9/1.2.10 fail intermittently with "The agent never sent a
SET_RESP".

Fix in two parts:
- nu_ipaddr.c: only compare addresses of the same family as the
  expected address; report has_addr=false when the expected family
  has no address (transient loss).
- stomp.c: in HandleStompSourceIPAddrChanges(), defer the connection
  restart while the interface address is transiently absent. The
  normal heartbeat/socket-error path still detects genuinely dead
  connections.

Bench-validated on prplWare 4.2.1 (Freedom platform): the previously
failing prpl_hl-api-cert.1.4 / prplos.1.2.9 / prplos.1.2.10 all pass,
with zero spurious connection restarts across the full trigger
sequence.

Fixes: PPW-1741
Signed-off-by: Zhang Junjie <zhangjunjie@actiontec.com>
---
 src/core/nu_ipaddr.c | 11 +++++++++++
 src/core/stomp.c     | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/nu_ipaddr.c b/src/core/nu_ipaddr.c
index af2f405..6536b4a 100644
--- a/src/core/nu_ipaddr.c
+++ b/src/core/nu_ipaddr.c
@@ -871,6 +871,11 @@ int nu_ipaddr_has_interface_addr_changed(char *dev, char *expected_addr, bool *h
     char *str;
     char buf[NU_IPADDRSTRLEN];       // Buffer used to contain the IP address of each interface found in turn
     bool result;
+    int expected_family;
+
+    // Only compare addresses of the same family as the expected address, else a
+    // remaining IPv6 address masks a transient IPv4 loss (eg during DHCP release/rebind)
+    expected_family = (strchr(expected_addr, ':') != NULL) ? AF_INET6 : AF_INET;
 
     // Exit if unable to get a linked list containing the IP Addresses of all network interfaces on the current system
     *has_addr = false;
@@ -903,6 +908,12 @@ int nu_ipaddr_has_interface_addr_changed(char *dev, char *expected_addr, bool *h
             continue;
         }
 
+        // Skip this result, if it is not the same address family as the expected address
+        if (family != expected_family)
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+
         // Determine pointer to IPv4 or IPv6 address
         if (family == AF_INET)
         {
diff --git a/src/core/stomp.c b/src/core/stomp.c
index 6790d11..fe0dc0a 100644
--- a/src/core/stomp.c
+++ b/src/core/stomp.c
@@ -3925,6 +3925,16 @@ void HandleStompSourceIPAddrChanges(void)
         if ((sc->instance != INVALID) && (sc->mgmt_if_name[0] != '\0') && (sc->mgmt_ip_addr[0] != '\0'))
         {
             has_changed = nu_ipaddr_has_interface_addr_changed(sc->mgmt_if_name, sc->mgmt_ip_addr, &has_addr);
+
+            // Ignore a transient loss of the address (eg during a DHCP release/rebind cycle):
+            // restarting here would drop queued USP messages for the whole reconnect window.
+            // A genuinely dead connection is still detected by the heartbeat/socket-error path.
+            if ((has_changed) && (has_addr == false))
+            {
+                USP_LOG_Warning("%s: Transient loss of address on %s - deferring restart of STOMP connection %d.", __FUNCTION__, sc->mgmt_if_name, sc->instance);
+                continue;
+            }
+
             if (has_changed)
             {
                 // Stop, then restart the STOMP connection
-- 
2.43.0

